    "prompt": "Vikunja task 1624 in project Gordon: Ship the thing\n\n<p>Make it so.</p>\n\nTask comments, fetched from the Vikunja API when the task was picked\nup: raw JSON, one object per comment, \"comment\" is HTML, \"created\" is\nits timestamp. The description plus these comments are the spec; when\nthey conflict, the later comment wins.\n\n<vikunja-comments>\n[{\"id\":1,\"comment\":\"<p>earlier</p>\",\"author\":{\"username\":\"eric\"}}]\n</vikunja-comments>\n\nIf that block is empty, the fetch failed: read the comments with the\nvikunja MCP tools instead.\n\nThe task's attachments were downloaded into `/workspace/attachments` when this\npod started, each as `<attachment id>-<file name>` (the id in the\ndescription's `.../attachments/<id>` image URLs). `/workspace/attachments/index.md`\nlists every attachment with its path or why it was skipped; no index means\nthe download failed. Read the ones the task relies on before planning (the\nRead tool shows images).\n\nOpen the pull request with `gh pr create --base main --label kelos:claude-opus --label kelos:fix-suggestions`:\nthe label routes `/gordon` follow-up comments on it\nback to the same agent type.\n`kelos:fix-suggestions` also has the review follow-ups fix the reviewers' suggestions\ntoo, not only their Blocking findings.\n\nThis pod may have waited for the tasks blocking this one after the\nrepository was cloned. Before starting, run `git fetch origin\n\"$KELOS_BASE_BRANCH\" && git merge --ff-only FETCH_HEAD`; if the\nmerge refuses because the branch already has its own commits, leave\nit as it is.\nThe model-free PR-open automation comments on Vikunja task\n1624 with the PR link; do not duplicate it.\n",
    "ttlSecondsAfterFinished": 259200,
